WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — ai-coding-market (90s) Narrator Osato

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:07.451
First, headline trillion-dollar figures for AI coding are future guesses, not counts of money already earned.

2
00:00:07.951 --> 00:00:14.778
Second, almost every forecast assumes developers will pay a giant AI model by the word forever.

3
00:00:15.278 --> 00:00:21.131
Third, saving and reusing working code drives repeated jobs toward electricity cost,

4
00:00:21.131 --> 00:00:23.360
making those forecasts too high.

5
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:28.832
At list prices, a single multi-step coding query can cost over two dollars and

6
00:00:28.832 --> 00:00:33.740
burn a thousand times more words than simple chat, even when extra words fail

7
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:40.432
to raise accuracy. Paying that bill forever on routine tasks ignores software's greatest strength: reuse.

8
00:00:40.932 --> 00:00:46.699
Our essay labels every published figure strictly by what it counts. Multiplying thirty million

9
00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:53.999
developers by one hundred thousand dollars yields a three-trillion-dollar value projection, whereas surveyed enterprise

10
00:00:53.999 --> 00:00:58.846
spend on AI coding tools in 2025 was four billion dollars across actual buyers.

11
00:00:59.346 --> 00:01:04.695
First, open weights and competition have cut the price of fixed benchmark capability

12
00:01:04.695 --> 00:01:11.319
roughly thirteenfold per year since 2023. Second, crystallizing checked answers into deterministic local

13
00:01:11.319 --> 00:01:16.732
routines slashes how many paid model calls each recurring software job even requires.

14
00:01:17.232 --> 00:01:22.436
Software creation can grow massively valuable for society and everyday builders while

15
00:01:22.436 --> 00:01:28.192
perpetual per-word vendor revenue compresses steadily toward the physical cost of electricity.
